# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit the real .env — it's already in .gitignore for the
# Supabase keys from the earlier backend design; add these alongside them.

# Vercel serverless functions read this for src/services/extraction (Phase 1) — image/PDF
# reading (vision-client.ts). This is a SEPARATE Gemini key from GEMINI_API_KEY below, which
# is used by the AI planning assistant elsewhere in the app. Keeping them separate means a
# heavy folder scan (site photos, PDFs) never eats into the assistant's quota, and vice versa.
GEMINI_EXTRACTION_API_KEY=

# The extraction models, in the order they are tried. A folder scan walks down this list: when a
# model reports its DAILY allowance spent, the run moves to the next one rather than leaving the
# rest of the folder unread. Daily caps are metered per model AND per provider, which is what
# makes the list worth having — a scan of 178 documents once stopped at 37 because one model's
# day ran out and there was nowhere else to go.
#
# Check what a key can actually reach before setting these. Availability varies by account, and
# several models named in published comparisons (gemini-3-flash, Llama 4 Scout) 404 on an
# ordinary key:
#   curl "https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models?key=$GEMINI_EXTRACTION_API_KEY"
#   curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $GROQ_API_KEY" https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/models
# GEMINI_EXTRACTION_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash
# GEMINI_EXTRACTION_MODEL_2=gemini-3.5-flash

# The last lane, and optional. Without it the chain is Gemini-only and a spent Gemini day stops
# the scan exactly as it used to. Must name a vision-capable model.
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_VISION_MODEL=qwen/qwen3.8-27b
# From the earlier backend design session — add these too if not already present.
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_KEY=
#GEMINI_API_KEY=
#GEMINI_REPLAN_MODEL=